      "path": "docs/research/free-content/README.md",
      "line": 85,
      "heading": "What the original checks established",
      "text": "Structured responses were obtained from Google Books (using the configured key), Open Library, Internet Archive, DOAJ, OpenAlex, Crossref, arXiv, Europe PMC, CORE, Zenodo, HAL, Wikisource, Library of Congress, and LibriVox. Gutenberg RDF and DOAB record/harvesting responses also worked. OAPEN's OAI service identification worked; a record import was not exercised.",
      "status": "historical-context-needs-reconciliation"
    },
    {
      "document_id": "a75437e3d72377932ea11a25802bb26f5d95f9cf44cee727809cf332c72ab952",
      "path": "docs/research/free-content/README.md",
      "line": 89,
      "heading": "What the original checks established",
      "text": "- An Open Library work returned `ebook_access: public` alongside many Internet Archive identifiers. That does not identify which edition is freely readable.\n- A HAL hit had a record URL and DOI but no `fileMain_s`: a repository hit is not necessarily full text.\n- Zenodo returned a dataset; item-type filtering is essential.\n- DOAJ supplied an older HTTP publisher URL; metadata alone does not prove the destination still works.\n- Semantic Scholar returned **429**, and Gutendex timed out. Those checks do not establish general service availability.\n- Some documentation URLs moved; corrected DOAB/OAPEN URLs appear in the catalog. Some sites returned only a JavaScript shell. NCERT/ERIC/OER Commons could not be fully inspected.",
      "status": "historical-context-needs-reconciliation"
    },
    {
      "document_id": "1c3d0752f7c6a4fd3fd60df7db6432123a281b127df0a2b4e3bbfbed3b9376a6",
      "path": "docs/research/free-content/BLOCKED_CONNECTOR_ACCESS_REPORT.md",
